+## Changed
+
+- `restartDefaultBranchBranch` now turns a failed `worktreeRemove` into the
+  `could not remove worktree <path>: <git's message>` error followed by the
+  recovery line, and stops before renaming the branch or touching the markers.
+- `approveDefaultBranchSteering` skips the `osq: <id> replanned` commit when
+  `vcs.status()` has no path under the change folder, so a second approval
+  after a failed restart no longer fails with `nothing to commit`.
+- Added `tests/recovery-restart-remove-fails.test.ts`, which proves "Worktree
+  removal fails during a restart" with `scenario`, including the unchanged
+  regression marker, the untouched branch, and the successful second approval.
+
